m/godotengine/godot/issues/101314#issuecomment-2580498659","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101314","id":2580498659,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zz0jj","user":{"login":"JoshuaSteward1193","id":31291387,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMjkxMzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31291387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193","html_url":"https://github.com/JoshuaSteward1193","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoshuaSteward1193/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T15:01:00Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T15:01:00Z","body":"> Can't reproduce (v4.3.stable.official [[77dcf97](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/77dcf97d82cbfe4e4615475fa52ca03da645dbd8)]). Have you pressed the \"Add Key/Value Pair\" button after entering the key/value? 🤔 ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce138016-ff09-4a54-8b51-c315eb50ab22)\n> \n> Also can't reproduce for typed Dictionary in v4.4.dev7.official [[46c8f8c](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/46c8f8c5c5874c7c56ea5b1384259de9402d3449)].\n\nAhh I see. To me I thought that was adding 'another' key value pair, not saving the one in the entry boxes above the button. For the arrays, there isn't an entry box for a new item until you click \"Add\", so I didn't think it worked differently for the key value pairs.\n\nThat being said, thanks for you explanation on how to properly use this.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580498659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2581451850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101314#issuecomment-2581451850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101314","id":2581451850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z3dRK","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T23:36:41Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T23:36:41Z","body":"From time by time i see someone get confused with this, shouldn't we change this for something more clear like `Save Key/Value Pair` or `Append Key/Value Pair`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2581451850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585379965","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101314#issuecomment-2585379965","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101314","id":2585379965,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aGcR9","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T19:12:36Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T19:12:36Z","body":"> From time by time i see someone get confused with this, shouldn't we change this for something more clear like `Save Key/Value Pair` or `Append Key/Value Pair`?\n\nIndeed this keeps confusing users, seems to be unintuitive (I think happened to me as well to forget to press that button). I think just changing the button text won't solve the actual issue though, it won't make you intuitively know that after entering the key/value you need to confirm / actually add such pair. 🤔\n\nConceptually I'd say it is a dialog inlined within the inspector (you pick key/value then need to confirm). But visually this \"dialog part\" (new key/value + button) doesn't stand out to me like a \"single thing\", it's somehow noisy:\n\n> ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce138016-ff09-4a54-8b51-c315eb50ab22)\n\nNot sure what would be a good solution here. Possibly adding some visual indicator for the button after anything is entered into new key/value fields? Like some warning icon / highlighting / etc.\nOr maybe somehow changing the layout? Like putting this whole \"dialog part\" within its own color border, and moving the \"Add new key/value\" into the first \"dialog-title\" row (+changing the button to \"confirm\")?\n(Again, not sure, just throwing some ideas...)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585379965/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585401399","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101314#issuecomment-2585401399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101314","id":2585401399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aGhg3","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T20:39:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T20:39:31Z","body":"Is not possible be like the other properties in the inspector? Just put the data and when you press `ctrl + s` the engine retrieve the data from the inspector and save.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585401399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585477830","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101314#issuecomment-2585477830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101314","id":2585477830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aG0LG","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T23:27:06Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T23:27:06Z","body":"> Is not possible be like the other properties in the inspector? Just put the data and when you press `ctrl + s` the engine retrieve the data from the inspector and save.\n\nThe thing is for \"other properties\" you edit them, they already exist. E.g. for Array you first add an element, which is automatically added at the end (no need to specify the index - it's implicit), then you edit the value for an already existing/in-array element. In case of Dictionary the custom keys are meant to be unique, they're not editable after adding key/value pair, only the value is editable. Hence the key needs to be specified before adding the key/value entry.\n\nTo me it doesn't make much sense to auto-add an entry on save. Note that the default no-key/null is a valid key that can be added... so if auto-adding-on-save would be a thing then shouldn't saving without any edits add a `null`/`null` entry? 🤔 Of course this case could be an exception (which would introduce inconsistency). But besides that the user might simply change their mind after entering some key/value, they might intentionally want to not add such entry for whatever reason. After saving they'd discover it was added (whoever knows how much time later). So such auto-adding seems to me rather as more potential confusion/problems.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585477830/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3067225486","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101314#issuecomment-3067225486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101314","id":3067225486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc620iWO","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T18:19:49Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T18:22:31Z","body":"I'm closing this since it isn't really about an issue anymore, but rather a discussion about changing behavior\n\nThere exists a [proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5775) that suggests changing this behavior, that has some decent traction.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3067225486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]